{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>After it.</b> Rashi explained: it is written in Joel, and the like of it was not before it — for there were many species. This is difficult, for in the book of Psalms it counts regarding the plague of locusts in Egypt: ילק וחסיל. One may say that nevertheless they were not as many species as in Joel. Or, in the days of Moses all the species came together at once, and what it says ואחריו לא יהיה כן — that means at once; but in the days of Joel they came one after another, as it is written: יתר הגזם אכל הארבה. And what is written וכמוהו לא היה לפניו — regarding גזם alone, there never was its like as it came in the days of Joel; and likewise regarding ארבה alone, and likewise regarding ילק alone."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:02:53.317558843Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}